Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.096 --> 00:00:02.599
- Fruits, fruits, fruits, fruits.

00:00:02.599 --> 00:00:06.025
Natural sugar is what this video's about.

00:00:06.997 --> 00:00:08.323
(upbeat tropical music)

00:00:09.185 --> 00:00:10.908
- Guava, oh I dropped it!

00:00:10.908 --> 00:00:12.275
- You can eat the rind of a guava?

00:00:12.275 --> 00:00:14.148
- I don't know if I wanna eat the rind.

00:00:14.148 --> 00:00:15.459
- Well do I eat the seeds?

00:00:15.459 --> 00:00:17.316
- You could bust up some
teeth with these seeds.

00:00:17.316 --> 00:00:18.222
- Ah!

00:00:18.222 --> 00:00:19.522
I like cracked a tooth there.

00:00:19.522 --> 00:00:21.048
- Oh my god, that is really good.

00:00:21.048 --> 00:00:22.366
- Guava me some more fruits.

00:00:23.224 --> 00:00:24.658
- [Voiceover] Tamarind!

00:00:24.658 --> 00:00:25.399
- Ooh!

00:00:25.399 --> 00:00:27.402
- The exoskeleton is very weak.

00:00:27.402 --> 00:00:28.792
- It looks like chocolate.

00:00:28.792 --> 00:00:29.450
(sniffs)

00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:30.887
But it smells like
these vitamins I used to

00:00:30.887 --> 00:00:32.408
give my pet lizard.

00:00:32.408 --> 00:00:33.766
- This looks really weird.

00:00:33.766 --> 00:00:35.119
Like it's veiny.

00:00:35.119 --> 00:00:37.441
- But it's like a really nice, sweet sap.

00:00:37.441 --> 00:00:39.656
- It has like a date, figgy taste.

00:00:39.656 --> 00:00:41.455
- Am I doing this right?

00:00:41.455 --> 00:00:42.482
- [Voiceover] Lychee.

00:00:42.482 --> 00:00:43.989
- Cracking open a can of eyeballs.

00:00:43.989 --> 00:00:45.379
- Kind of reminds me of those fruit snacks

00:00:45.379 --> 00:00:46.344
my mom used to pack.

00:00:46.344 --> 00:00:48.266
- These taste so much
better than they look.

00:00:48.266 --> 00:00:50.352
You could definitely sip
up the juices in this can.

00:00:50.352 --> 00:00:51.504
- Ooh that's good.

00:00:51.504 --> 00:00:52.612
I like that a lot.

00:00:52.612 --> 00:00:54.104
- Oh my gosh, that's incredible.

00:00:54.104 --> 00:00:55.944
It's like a pineapple but better.

00:00:55.944 --> 00:00:58.203
- Lychee desserts, like a lychee pie.

00:00:58.203 --> 00:00:59.149
Has anyone done that?

00:00:59.149 --> 00:01:00.471
Will somebody do that?

00:01:00.471 --> 00:01:01.846
Should I do that?

00:01:01.846 --> 00:01:03.079
- [Voiceover] Dragon fruit.

00:01:03.079 --> 00:01:04.597
- This is not fruit, this is art.

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:06.114
- This is the fruit that everyone should

00:01:06.114 --> 00:01:07.594
Instagram themselves eating.

00:01:07.594 --> 00:01:09.432
- This is giving me like kiwi vibes.

00:01:09.432 --> 00:01:10.788
- It takes me to the ocean.

00:01:10.788 --> 00:01:12.412
- Please don't judge me.

00:01:12.412 --> 00:01:14.179
- It's kinda like all show, no flavor.

00:01:14.179 --> 00:01:16.108
- It's good, I just feel
like I'm eating air.

00:01:16.108 --> 00:01:18.093
- By looks though, this takes the cake.

00:01:18.093 --> 00:01:19.324
I need to decorate my place so

00:01:19.324 --> 00:01:20.435
if you have some more of these

00:01:20.435 --> 00:01:22.666
I'll just put them in
various places in my house.

00:01:22.666 --> 00:01:26.332
- Jackfruit named after Jack?

00:01:26.332 --> 00:01:27.514
- What's up with all these cans?

00:01:28.448 --> 00:01:30.446
- Oh ugh, it's kind of aggressive.

00:01:30.446 --> 00:01:31.677
- It's a little rubbery.

00:01:31.677 --> 00:01:33.086
- Let's see how its juice is.

00:01:33.086 --> 00:01:34.900
- Taste-wise, it's really good.

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:36.355
- No, I like the lychee better.

00:01:36.355 --> 00:01:39.030
- Now Stevefruit would
probably be pretty good.

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:39.980
- [Voiceover] Dude what is that?

00:01:39.980 --> 00:01:42.344
- It's like a fruit mush
wrapped in a condom.

00:01:42.344 --> 00:01:43.410
- This is a fruit?

00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:45.425
- This is just making
me sad, looking at this.

00:01:45.425 --> 00:01:46.919
- It smells like rotten cantaloupe.

00:01:46.919 --> 00:01:48.270
- It smells like garlic.

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:49.090
- I don't like that.

00:01:49.090 --> 00:01:50.320
Can I have a lychee please?

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:52.370
- Well actually it's grown on me.

00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:53.928
Ooh it's got a great aftertaste.

00:01:53.928 --> 00:01:55.200
- This is like really good.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:56.350
- I'm pleasantly surprised.

00:01:56.350 --> 00:01:57.333
You know what?

00:01:57.333 --> 00:01:59.250
Good things come in nasty packages.

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:02.280
Okay.

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:03.300
- [Voiceover] Oh yes!

